# nuts goals — what the current work is for.
#
# A goal claims an identity prefix: every task whose identity starts with it
# belongs to the goal. `nuts jj snapshot --goal "..."` then commits exactly
# those tasks, titled after the goal.
#
# done: all | any | manual — when the goal counts as reached. It never decides
# whether a commit happens, only whether nuts calls the goal satisfied.

